# Copy to .env and fill in. Everything the pipeline needs to pick a provider and a model lives
# here -- nothing about model choice should require editing code, because the caches are keyed by
# provider and model name and a code edit silently orphans every previous run.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Credentials. One is enough.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...              # https://aistudio.google.com/apikey  (free tier)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# HF_TOKEN=hf_...
# ALIBABA_CLOUD_API_KEY=sk-...
# ALIBABA_BASE_URL=https://<your-workspace>.<region>.maas.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
#   a dedicated Alibaba workspace answers on its own host, not the shared dashscope one
# (no key at all -> local Ollama on http://localhost:11434)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Which provider to use. Optional: without it the first credential found wins, in the order
#    anthropic -> gemini -> huggingface -> alibaba -> ollama.
#    Pin it when several keys are present, so adding a key does not silently switch providers.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COVENANT_BACKEND=gemini         # anthropic | gemini | huggingface | alibaba | ollama

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Which models. Optional: each provider has a sensible default pair.
#    "small"   -- per-document classification and per-transaction categorisation (many cheap calls)
#    "complex" -- reading the KYC/audit text against the ledger, and building the covenant specs
#                 (few calls, but this is where model quality decides the score)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated: the first name is the model of record (it keys the caches), the rest are
# fallen through to as each one's daily quota runs out. On a free tier one model cannot carry a
# run of ~115 calls, but several in a chain can.
# COVENANT_MODEL_SMALL=gemini-2.5-flash,gemini-2.5-flash-lite,gemini-3.1-flash-lite,gemma-4-31b-it
# COVENANT_MODEL_COMPLEX=gemini-3.5-flash,gemini-3-flash-preview,gemma-4-31b-it
#
# Gemini free tier, measured rather than documented: each model allows about twenty requests per
# day and they are metered separately, and every *-pro model reports `limit: 0` -- they are not available on the free tier at all,
# nor is gemini-2.0-flash. Usable, fastest first:
#   gemini-2.5-flash-lite, gemini-3.1-flash-lite   ~0.9s   cheapest, fine for classification
#   gemini-3.5-flash, gemini-3-flash-preview       ~1.2s
#   gemini-2.5-flash                               ~1.5s
#   gemma-4-31b-it                                 ~2.1s
#   gemini-3.6-flash                              ~28s     heavy internal reasoning, slow
# Splitting the two tiers across two different models also splits the quota across them.
#
# A model whose *daily* allowance is spent is remembered for the rest of the run and skipped, so
# the chain costs one refused request per model, not one before every call. A per-minute 429 is
# not treated that way -- it is waited out, because it reopens.
#
# Ollama (local): qwen2.5:7b-instruct, qwen2.5:14b-instruct. Avoid the qwen3 line -- Ollama serves
# it with a generic chat template, so thinking cannot be switched off and the whole token budget
# goes to invisible reasoning.

# The strongest model available should carry the "complex" tier: that is where the spec, the term
# binding and the review pass live, and those three are the whole difference between a cell that
# is right and one that is plausible. Only the tiers' model names change -- nothing else does.
# COVENANT_BACKEND=alibaba
# COVENANT_MODEL_COMPLEX=qwen3-max
# COVENANT_MODEL_SMALL=qwen3-8b
# ALIBABA_BASE_URL=https://<your-workspace>.<region>.maas.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Endpoint override. Rarely needed: point the selected backend at a different OpenAI-compatible
#    host (a private gateway, a proxy, a self-hosted server).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COVENANT_BASE_URL=https://your-gateway.example.com/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Throughput. COVENANT_CONCURRENCY is how many documents / scenarios are worked on at once
#    (default 4); COVENANT_MIN_INTERVAL is the minimum seconds between requests, shared across all
#    of them. On a rate-limited free tier the interval is the real constraint and concurrency only
#    parallelises the waiting -- set the interval to 0 on a paid endpoint and concurrency becomes
#    what actually lets a slower, better model finish inside the submission window.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COVENANT_CONCURRENCY=4
# COVENANT_MIN_INTERVAL=4.5
